fix: update wrangler.toml with alias for Hono subpath imports

Wrapping up migration to Cloudflare Workers. All business logic migrated:
- Express → Hono
- Drizzle ORM → raw SQL via @neondatabase/serverless
- jsonwebtoken → jose
- @node-rs/argon2 → bcryptjs
- Schema types → TypeScript interfaces

NOTE: Wrangler bundling needs [alias] table for Hono subpath imports
('hono/cors', 'hono/logger', 'hono/factory'). Install Vite + @cloudflare/vite-plugin
for better bundling support if wrangler --local doesn't work.

See: https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/6851
